WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.480
The school teaching and its practical requirements remain the course spine. Nancy supplies the learner-confirmed main textbook explanation, but it does not replace the eleven separate reading rows.
学校教学及实操要求仍是课程主线。Nancy 提供学习者确认的主要考试教材解释，但不取代另列十一项阅读。

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:24.816
The reading view below contains paired English and Chinese guides for every Week One reading row. Each names its actual source and separates the assigned locator from what has been source-read and taught.
下方阅读视图为第一周每项阅读列出中英对照讲解，分别标明实际来源，并区分学校指定位置与已源读、已讲解部分。

00:00:24.816 --> 00:00:47.208
The recovered school A&P copy now confirms the assigned Chapter 1 and 22 page ranges. The downloaded 2018 CPSC edition differs from the older page map for Chapter 9; the guide shows the intended glucometer topic and preserves the discrepancy. Other source or edition gaps remain explicitly flagged.
已找回的学校A&P版本现已核对第1、22章指定页范围。下载的2018版CPSC与较早版第9章页码表不同；本指南讲解意图中的血糖仪主题并保留差异。其他来源或版本缺口仍会明确标注。

00:00:47.208 --> 00:01:00.480
All explanations and practice cases here are newly written. Necessary clinical concepts may overlap another course, but no essential explanation requires the old ninety-five-lesson website.
这里解释及练习案例均为新写。必要临床概念可能与其他课程重合，但任何核心解释都不要求先去旧九十五课网站。

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:12.336
Homeostasis is dynamic regulation, not a frozen perfect number. A regulated variable can fluctuate while control systems work to keep it within a workable range.
稳态是动态调节，不是冻结在一个完美数字。控制系统维持可用范围时，受调节变量仍会波动。

00:01:12.336 --> 00:01:25.440
In negative feedback, the response opposes the disturbance. A rising body temperature can stimulate heat-loss responses such as sweating and increased skin blood flow when the environment permits heat loss.
负反馈的响应与扰动方向相反。体温上升可刺激出汗及皮肤血流增加等散热反应，但效果依赖环境能否散热。

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:36.792
Positive feedback amplifies a process toward an endpoint, as in platelet recruitment during clot formation. Positive does not mean beneficial and negative does not mean harmful.
正反馈将过程放大直至终点，例如凝血中的血小板募集。正不等于有益，负不等于有害。

00:01:36.792 --> 00:01:49.320
For assessment, ask which variable is threatened, what compensation you can observe and whether the system is succeeding. A normal number may be maintained at a high physiological cost.
评估时问哪个变量受威胁、能观察到什么代偿、系统是否成功。正常数字可能以很高生理代价维持。

00:01:49.320 --> 00:02:01.536
Pressure depends on flow and vascular resistance. If effective circulating volume falls, compensatory increases in heart rate and vascular tone may temporarily support pressure.
压力依赖血流和血管阻力。有效循环量下降时，代偿性心率及血管张力增加，可暂时支持血压。

00:02:01.536 --> 00:02:14.952
That compensation helps explain a rising pulse and cool skin before overt hypotension. It does not prove hemorrhage: pain, fever, drugs and other causes can produce overlapping findings.
这帮助解释明显低血压前出现的脉快及皮肤凉，但不能证明出血；疼痛、发热、药物等也可产生重叠发现。

00:02:14.952 --> 00:02:27.576
Link serial findings rather than diagnosing from one clue. A worsening mental state, respiratory effort and pressure trend can show that the patient is no longer compensating adequately.
应联系连续发现，不凭一个线索诊断。意识、呼吸功及血压趋势恶化，可提示患者已无法充分代偿。

00:02:27.576 --> 00:02:38.904
The practical consequence is earlier reassessment, escalation and definitive-care planning. It is not permission to give the same fluid volume to every patient with a fast pulse.
实际后果是更早复评、升级及安排确定性照护，而不是允许所有脉快者都给同一补液体积。

00:02:38.904 --> 00:02:51.720
Conducting airways bring gas toward the respiratory zone. The main gas-exchange surface is the thin alveolar-capillary interface, where oxygen and carbon dioxide move down partial-pressure gradients.
传导气道把气体送向呼吸区。主要交换面是薄的肺泡毛细血管界面，氧与二氧化碳沿分压梯度移动。

00:02:51.720 --> 00:03:05.448
During ordinary inspiration, respiratory muscles enlarge the chest and create the pressure difference that draws air in. Narrowed airways increase resistance and can make expiration particularly difficult.
普通吸气时，呼吸肌扩大胸腔，形成吸入空气的压差。气道变窄增加阻力，可使呼气尤其困难。

00:03:05.448 --> 00:03:19.824
Not all inspired volume reaches gas-exchanging alveoli. Rapid tiny breaths can move much of their volume through dead space, so a normal-looking minute volume or respiratory rate may hide poor alveolar ventilation.
吸入体积并非全到交换肺泡。快速极浅呼吸可能大多在死腔内移动，所以看似正常分钟通气量或频率，可能掩盖肺泡通气不足。

00:03:19.824 --> 00:03:32.736
Gas exchange also needs matching blood flow and a usable membrane. More oxygen concentration cannot by itself repair every ventilation, perfusion or diffusion problem.
气体交换还需要匹配血流和可用膜。提高氧浓度本身不能修复所有通气、灌注或弥散问题。

00:03:32.736 --> 00:03:46.704
A satisfactory saturation describes only one part of oxygen transport. A person may lack enough hemoglobin, sufficient cardiac output or effective tissue use despite a high displayed saturation.
满意饱和度只描述氧运输一部分。即使显示高，患者仍可能缺足够血红蛋白、心输出量或有效组织利用。

00:03:46.704 --> 00:04:00.816
Carbon monoxide illustrates several broken links: reduced available hemoglobin carriage, impaired release of remaining oxygen and cellular effects. A two-wavelength saturation cannot resolve those problems.
CO 展示多个链节受损：可用血红蛋白携氧减少、剩余氧释放受限及细胞影响。双波长饱和度不能解决这些问题。

00:04:00.816 --> 00:04:13.920
Compare this with hypoventilation on supplemental oxygen, where saturation may improve while carbon dioxide rises. You still need respiratory observation and appropriate capnography.
再比较吸氧下通气不足：饱和度可能改善，二氧化碳却上升。因此仍需呼吸观察及适当二氧化碳监测。

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:25.104
Use the mechanism to select the next assessment and support, not to chase one normal number. Document which link you believe is threatened and the evidence supporting that concern.
用机制选择下一评估和支持，而不是追一个正常数字。记录认为哪个链节受威胁，以及支持担忧的证据。

00:04:25.104 --> 00:04:35.520
Heart sounds are timed mechanical events. S one is associated with atrioventricular valve closure as ventricular pressure rises at the start of systole.
心音是有时序的机械事件。S1 与心室压力在收缩初升高时，房室瓣关闭相关。

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:48.336
S two is associated with aortic and pulmonic closure as ventricular pressure falls at the end of systole. The interval from S one to S two is systolic; the next interval is diastolic.
S2 与收缩末心室压力下降时，主动脉瓣及肺动脉瓣关闭相关。S1到S2为收缩期，接下来到下个S1为舒张期。

00:04:48.336 --> 00:05:01.488
Normal inspiration can widen the audible separation of the two components of S two. Splitting varies with physiology and disease; hearing a split does not automatically diagnose a valve disorder.
正常吸气可使 S2 两组分可闻分离增宽。分裂受生理及疾病影响，听到分裂不自动诊断瓣膜病。

00:05:01.488 --> 00:05:12.096
Relating a sound to the pulse and cycle is more useful than memorizing lub-dub alone. In a moving ambulance, noise can make subtle timing unreliable.
把声音与脉搏及心动周期对应，比只记“咚嗒”有用。行驶救护车噪声会使细微时序不可靠。

00:05:12.096 --> 00:05:25.488
S three follows S two in early diastole and is associated with rapid ventricular filling. It can be physiological in some contexts, but can also accompany volume loading or ventricular dysfunction.
S3 在 S2 后的舒张早期，与快速心室充盈相关。某些背景可属生理，也可伴容量负荷或心室功能障碍。

00:05:25.488 --> 00:05:38.064
S four occurs before S one in late diastole, linked to atrial contraction against a less compliant ventricle. A coordinated atrial contraction is needed for that classic mechanism.
S4 在 S1 前的舒张晚期，与心房向顺应性低的心室收缩相关。这种经典机制需要协调心房收缩。

00:05:38.064 --> 00:05:52.008
These are typically low-frequency sounds, unlike many higher-frequency clicks. The candidate text uses an inconsistent high-pitch description for abnormal S three; do not memorize that as the defining feature.
它们通常是低频声音，与许多高频喀喇音不同。候选教材对异常 S3 使用不一致的高频描述，不能把它背成定义。

00:05:52.008 --> 00:06:04.632
Integrate an extra sound with breathlessness, perfusion, history and other findings. Do not turn a possibly missed or uncertain gallop into a positive or negative diagnosis.
额外心音应结合气促、灌注、病史及其他发现。不能把可能漏听或不确定的奔马律，硬变成阳性或阴性诊断。

00:06:04.632 --> 00:06:18.480
Use the taught auscultation sites and a suitable stethoscope surface. The diaphragm generally transmits higher-frequency sounds and the lightly applied bell can help with lower-frequency sounds, depending on the instrument.
使用所教听诊部位及适当听诊面。膜面通常传高频，轻贴钟面可帮助听低频，具体也依设备而定。

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:30.624
First establish the basic sounds and their relation to the cycle. A murmur is a prolonged flow-related sound and must be described by timing and location rather than renamed S three.
先识别基本心音及周期关系。杂音是持续的血流相关声，应按时相和部位描述，不能改叫 S3。

00:06:30.624 --> 00:06:43.512
Auscultation expertise requires supervised listening to validated examples and real examinations. A text description or a synthetic sound cannot certify that you can distinguish heart sounds.
听诊能力需要督导下听经验证示例及真实检查。文字或合成声音不能证明你已能区分心音。

00:06:43.512 --> 00:06:56.448
If noise prevents a reliable examination, record that limit and use the other relevant evidence. Do not delay urgent care while repeatedly trying to hear a subtle sound in an unsuitable environment.
噪声使检查不可靠时，应记录局限，并使用其他相关证据。不要在不适合环境反复追听细音，延误紧急照护。

00:06:56.448 --> 00:07:09.504
Infection prevention is not just putting on gloves. Pathogens can move from a patient to hands, equipment, a phone or another patient when contaminated surfaces are carried into clean work.
感染预防不只是戴手套。污染表面进入洁净工作时，病原可从患者转至手、设备、手机或另一患者。

00:07:09.504 --> 00:07:22.800
Select precautions from the patient, task, anticipated splash and transmission route. Eye protection, a gown or an appropriate mask or respirator answer different exposure risks.
按患者、任务、预期飞溅及传播途径选择防护。护目、隔离衣及适当口罩或呼吸防护器，对应不同暴露风险。

00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:36.240
Clean technique reduces contamination; sterile technique maintains a sterile field for procedures that require it. Clean gloves are not sterile gloves, and disinfection of a cuff is not sterilization.
清洁技术减少污染；无菌技术为所需操作维持无菌区。清洁手套不是无菌手套，袖带消毒也不是灭菌。

00:07:36.240 --> 00:07:48.432
Use approved hand-hygiene products and the applicable procedure, including soap and water when required. Clean shared measurement equipment between patients and keep dirty and clean items separate.
使用获准手卫生产品并遵守适用规程，需要时用肥皂清水。患者之间清洁共用测量设备，并分开脏净物品。

00:07:48.432 --> 00:08:04.464
The archived Canadian CPSC checklist gives a gown, mask or respirator, eye protection and glove sequence after hand hygiene. Treat it as a named teaching checklist and verify the current school or service sequence for the equipment used.
存档加拿大 CPSC 清单在手卫生后列隔离衣、口罩或呼吸防护器、护目、手套顺序。它是特定教学清单，使用时仍核实学校或机构对当前器械的顺序。

00:08:04.464 --> 00:08:16.608
Choose equipment before contact and check size and integrity. A respirator requires the applicable fit-testing and seal-check procedure; a loose mask is not equivalent protection.
接触前选择设备、检查尺寸及完整性。呼吸防护器需要适用适合性测试和密合检查，松口罩不能等同保护。

00:08:16.608 --> 00:08:27.264
Ordinary glasses are not a substitute for suitable eye protection. Where a gown is indicated, ensure the coverage and glove-cuff interface match the taught technique.
普通眼镜不能代替适当护目。需要隔离衣时，确保覆盖及手套袖口连接符合所教技术。

00:08:27.264 --> 00:08:40.104
In the school station, explain which hazard each item addresses and demonstrate without touching contaminated areas. Extra equipment worn incorrectly can create another removal hazard.
学校站点中解释每件防哪种风险，示范时避免接触污染区。额外设备若穿戴错误，会增加脱除危险。

00:08:40.104 --> 00:08:53.016
The archived checklist removes gloves, cleans hands, removes the gown, cleans hands, then removes eye and respiratory protection using appropriate handling points, followed by hand hygiene.
存档清单为脱手套、手卫生、脱隔离衣、手卫生，再从适当拿取点脱护目和呼吸防护，最后手卫生。

00:08:53.016 --> 00:09:07.560
Do not touch the front of the mask or shield, or drag a contaminated gown across clothing. The correct removal area matters, especially when respiratory protection must remain on until outside the exposure area.
不要碰口罩护面正面，也不要把污染隔离衣拖过衣服。脱除地点很重要，尤其呼吸防护需要离开暴露区域后才脱时。

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:20.160
Follow the actual current equipment-specific procedure if it differs. In practice, pause and correct an identified contamination rather than quickly finishing the remaining sequence with dirty hands.
若当前具体设备规程不同，应遵守实际规程。练习发现污染时应停下纠正，不能带着脏手赶完后续步骤。

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:32.568
Report a sharps or mucosal exposure promptly and follow occupational procedures. Wash or irrigate as appropriate; do not squeeze an injury or put bleach into a wound.
锐器或黏膜暴露应及时报告并按职业暴露流程处理。按需清洗冲洗，不要挤伤口或把漂白剂放进伤口。

00:09:32.568 --> 00:09:49.200
The Clinical Judgment Measurement Model names six functions: recognize cues, analyze cues, prioritize hypotheses, generate solutions, take action and evaluate outcomes. It is a reasoning framework, not a BC medication protocol.
临床判断测量模型列六功能：识别线索、分析线索、排列假设优先、生成方案、采取行动、评估结果。它是推理框架，不是卑诗用药流程。

00:09:49.200 --> 00:10:01.296
Recognition asks what is relevant; analysis asks how the findings fit together and what is missing. Prioritization balances likelihood, severity and time sensitivity.
识别问什么相关；分析问发现如何联系、还缺什么；优先排列兼顾可能性、严重性及时间紧迫性。

00:10:01.296 --> 00:10:13.704
Generate a plan with expected outcomes and separate indicated from contraindicated or nonessential tasks. Then act within the actual training, authorization and available resources.
拟定计划及预期结果，区分有适应证、有禁忌和非必要任务，再在实际训练、权限及资源范围内行动。

00:10:13.704 --> 00:10:23.400
Evaluation compares what happened with what should have happened. An unexpected response reopens the earlier reasoning rather than being edited out of the story.
评估将实际与预期比较。出乎意料的反应应重新打开前面的推理，而不是从故事中删掉。

00:10:23.400 --> 00:10:36.384
A stigmatizing label can change what you notice and what the patient is willing to share. Describe behaviour and attributed symptoms instead of replacing assessment with difficult, drunk or attention seeking.
污名标签会改变你注意什么，以及患者愿分享什么。应描述行为和有来源症状，不要用“难搞、醉了、求关注”取代评估。

00:10:36.384 --> 00:10:48.144
Therapeutic communication uses active listening, clarification and professional boundaries. Ask what matters to the person, explain what is happening and offer realistic choices.
治疗性沟通使用主动倾听、澄清及专业边界。询问对方重视什么，解释正在发生什么，并提供真实可选项。

00:10:48.144 --> 00:11:00.096
Team psychological safety means a student can state uncertainty or a safety concern without humiliation. It does not eliminate accountability or promise absolute confidentiality.
团队心理安全意味着学生可以表达不确定或安全担忧而不受羞辱，但不取消责任，也不承诺绝对保密。

00:11:00.096 --> 00:11:10.728
Use reflection and feedback to identify a blind spot. You do not have to disclose personal trauma to demonstrate insight or to participate safely in a case discussion.
用反思及反馈识别盲点。证明有洞察力或安全参与讨论，并不要求披露个人创伤。

00:11:10.728 --> 00:11:22.296
Use an original older-adult fall variant. The first reading question is not which textbook chapter to recite; it is what the new confusion and rising respiratory rate might mean.
用原创老年跌倒变式。首个阅读问题不是该背哪章，而是新发混乱和呼吸频率上升意味着什么。

00:11:22.296 --> 00:11:35.640
Connect mechanisms with observations: compensation may preserve pressure, while infection or metabolic illness may alter breathing and consciousness. Injury and illness can coexist.
把机制与观察联系：代偿可能保留血压，感染或代谢疾病可能改变呼吸意识。受伤与疾病可以并存。

00:11:35.640 --> 00:11:48.264
Use the reasoning functions to gather relevant data, challenge a simple mechanical-fall label, choose immediate support and plan safe movement. Do not force a diagnosis from an isolated score.
用推理功能收集相关数据，质疑简单“机械性跌倒”标签，选择即时支持并规划安全搬运。不能从孤立评分强推诊断。

00:11:48.264 --> 00:12:01.008
Finish with the actual serial values, response and unresolved concern. The useful product of reading is a better examination and decision, not a longer list of memorized definitions.
最终交接实际连续数值、反应及未解决担忧。阅读的有用成果是更好检查及决定，不是更长的定义背诵表。

00:12:01.008 --> 00:12:14.400
Active retrieval means producing an answer before reopening the material. Explain why shallow rapid breathing can fail, or calculate the complete NEWS2, rather than recognizing a highlighted phrase.
主动提取是重看资料前先产出答案。解释浅快呼吸为何可能无效，或完整计算 NEWS2，而不是只认出高亮句。

00:12:14.400 --> 00:12:26.712
Change one variable in a case: oxygen added, new confusion, a different tubing factor or a pulse that no longer matches the monitor. State how the decision changes and why.
在案例中只改变一个变量：加氧、新发混乱、不同滴系数，或脉搏不再匹配监护。说出决定怎样变、为什么。

00:12:26.712 --> 00:12:37.224
Then check the explanation and original locator. An error log should name the misconception, such as forgetting oxygen points, not merely say study harder.
随后核对解释及原文位置。错题记录应写具体误解，例如漏补氧分，而不是只写“更努力学习”。

00:12:37.224 --> 00:12:48.576
Repeat later with a different example and demonstrate skills under supervision. Memory practice improves retention but cannot certify physical technique or clinical competence.
稍后换例再测，并在督导下展示技能。记忆练习帮助保持，但不能认证操作技术或临床能力。

00:12:48.576 --> 00:13:30.888
Unstable adult: physiological and medical findings. The assigned examination list includes altered consciousness, inability to maintain an airway, respiratory distress or arrest, absent radial pulses, cardiac arrest, bleeding requiring a tourniquet or packing, and cool/pale/clammy skin with suspected shock. It also names suspected stroke, heat stroke, severe hypothermia, suspected cardiac chest pain and anaphylaxis. Thus unstable is not shorthand for a low blood pressure or for trauma alone. State which finding creates urgency and what support and destination planning must begin.
成人不稳定：生理及内科发现。指定考试清单包括意识改变、气道难维持、呼吸窘迫或停止、桡脉未触及、心脏骤停、需止血带或填塞的出血，以及疑休克伴凉白湿皮肤。也列疑卒中、热射病、严重低温、疑心源性胸痛及过敏反应。因此“不稳定”不只指低血压或创伤。应说明哪个发现造成紧迫性，以及须开始何种支持和目的地计划。

00:13:30.888 --> 00:14:12.816
Unstable adult: chest, pelvis and limbs. Recognize an unstable/deformed chest wall, an unstable pelvis, two or more proximal long-bone fractures, a crushed/degloved/mangled extremity, or amputation proximal to a wrist or ankle. The historical list also identifies a pulseless limb when one realignment attempt has not restored circulation. That wording is an examination criterion, not permission to manipulate any injury or repeat attempts. Describe distal circulation/sensation/movement and follow the actual trained fracture pathway.
成人不稳定：胸盆及肢体。识别胸壁不稳定或变形、骨盆不稳定、至少两处近端长骨骨折、挤压脱套毁损肢体，或腕踝近端截断。旧清单也列一次复位尝试仍无循环的无脉肢体。此措辞为考试标准，不授权任意操作或反复复位。应描述远端循环、感觉、运动，并遵真实受训骨折流程。

00:14:12.816 --> 00:14:51.624
Do not infer a foreign body from absent breathing alone. The old intervention table places absent respiration under obstructed-airway actions as well as ventilation. In practice assess patency, respiratory effort, air movement and the whole presentation: apnea can have other causes. Suction addresses fluids; manual opening and appropriate adjuncts address patency; assisted ventilation addresses inadequate movement of gas. CPR assessment follows the trained arrest process, not a prolonged search for a particular pulse while the person is clearly in arrest.
不能只凭无呼吸推定异物。旧干预表把无呼吸同时列在梗阻处理及通气下。实际须评通畅、呼吸努力、气流及整体表现；呼吸暂停可有其他原因。吸引处理液体，手法和适用辅具维护通畅，辅助通气处理气体移动不足。CPR评估遵受训骤停流程，不在明显骤停时长久寻找某一脉搏。

00:14:51.624 --> 00:15:32.400
AVPU names responsiveness, not airway certainty. A is spontaneously alert; V responds to voice; P responds only to an appropriate pressure/pain stimulus; U has no response. The source links reduced response with increasing airway concern and positions the patient according to injuries and needs. Even an alert person may have airway bleeding or nausea; do not assume A guarantees protection. Explain the actual response, monitor the airway and reassess. Do not use repeated injurious stimulation or equate AVPU with a full GCS or decision-making capacity.
AVPU标反应，不保证气道。A自发清醒，V对声音反应，P仅对适当压力或痛刺激反应，U无反应。来源将反应下降与气道担忧相联，按伤情需要摆位。清醒者也可能口腔出血或恶心，不能认为A保证保护。应描述真实反应、监护气道并复评。不反复用致伤刺激，也不把AVPU当完整GCS或决定能力。

00:15:32.400 --> 00:16:03.336
PCR: action boxes need context. The form groups care given, airway actions, oxygen device/flow, pain assessment and pupils. Record actual treatment, timing, delivery and response rather than ticking everything available. For pupils preserve right/left findings and what was tested; do not claim accommodation from a light reaction alone. A device label does not establish delivered oxygen concentration or effective ventilation.
PCR：行动格需背景。表分照护、气道、给氧设备流量、疼痛及瞳孔。记真处理、时点、输送和反应，不是可勾皆勾。瞳孔保左右及实际测试，不能仅光反射就写调节反应。设备名称也不证明实际吸氧浓度或有效通气。

00:16:03.336 --> 00:16:41.304
PCR: serial rows make change visible. Each timed row has GCS eye/verbal/motor components and total, pulse, respirations, SpO2, blood glucose, temperature, blood pressure, skin and protocols. Include relevant oxygen/device, measurement site and limitations in the available notes when needed. Never invent a diastolic pressure after a palpated systolic reading. Additional treatments/comments preserve the observation-decision-action-response timeline and information that does not fit the boxes.
PCR：连续行显示变化。各时刻行有GCS睁眼语言运动及总分、脉搏、呼吸、血氧、血糖、体温、血压、皮肤和规程。按需在备注记给氧设备、测量部位及局限。触诊仅得收缩压时不能编舒张压。额外处理评论保留观察、决定、行动、反应时间线及格内放不下的信息。

00:16:41.304 --> 00:17:29.736
Appendix: products and solutions. ASA is acetylsalicylic acid/aspirin, Nitro nitroglycerin, OTC over-the-counter, Tab tablet and Rx medication/prescription in this context. NS/N/S is normal saline; D5W and D10W are 5% and 10% dextrose in water. O2 is oxygen, CO2 carbon dioxide, H2O water and Hg mercury. The printed N2O2 entry is wrong for nitrous oxide: N2O is the correct formula, and Entonox is an oxygen/nitrous-oxide mixture, not pure nitrous oxide. A concentration or brand name is not a dose.
附录：药品溶液。ASA乙酰水杨酸或阿司匹林，Nitro硝酸甘油，OTC非处方，Tab片剂，Rx在此为药物或处方。NS/N/S生理盐水，D5W及D10W为5%、10%葡萄糖水。O2氧，CO2二氧化碳，H2O水，Hg汞。原N2O2错误，一氧化二氮应为N2O；Entonox为氧与一氧化二氮混合物，不是纯一氧化二氮。浓度品牌不等剂量。

00:17:29.736 --> 00:18:09.168
Appendix: legacy and ambiguous language needs repair. IDDM/NIDDM mean the old insulin-dependent/non-insulin-dependent diabetes categories; they must not be used to infer modern diabetes type from current treatment. AOB means alcohol on breath, not proven intoxication or an explanation for reduced consciousness. Ca is listed as cancer but can mean calcium elsewhere. OD/od is used for overdose/once daily, and Tx for treatment/transmit. Write the intended meaning; capitalization alone is not an adequate safety barrier.
附录：旧词及歧义须修正。IDDM/NIDDM为旧胰岛素依赖或非依赖类别，不可从当前治疗推现代糖尿病类型。AOB呼气酒味，不证明醉酒，也不解释意识下降。Ca此列癌症，别处可指钙。OD/od列过量或每日一次，Tx治疗或传输。应写本意，不能只靠大小写保障安全。

00:18:09.168 --> 00:18:36.768
Biologic and biosimilar. Biologics are complex products from living systems; a biosimilar is highly similar to an authorized reference biologic, with no expected clinically meaningful safety or efficacy difference on the supporting comparison. It is not simply a small-molecule generic or an untested imitation. This corrects the source text's misleading synthetically-produced and lesser-testing shorthand.
生物药与类似药。生物药是活系统产生的复杂制剂；生物类似药与获准参照药高度类似，支持比较中预期无临床有意义安全疗效差异。它不只是小分子仿制药，也不是未测试仿品。这修正原文“合成产生”及较少测试的误导概括。

00:18:36.768 --> 00:19:12.120
Repair the biologic example, not only its label. Printed11 calls etanercept a monoclonal antibody. The regulatory product information identifies it as a TNF-receptor/Fc fusion protein; it can bind TNF without being that antibody class. A biologic is not automatically less toxic or free from allergy/infection risks. Knowing the broad origin helps classify it, while the actual product information determines its properties. No maintenance-drug change follows from this classroom correction.
不只改生物药标签，也要修例子。印刷11页把依那西普称单克隆抗体，监管产品资料认定它为TNF受体与Fc融合蛋白，可结合TNF却不属于该抗体类别。生物药不自动毒性更低或无过敏感染风险。广义来源帮助分类，具体性质依真实产品资料。此课堂纠错不产生维持药调整指示。

00:19:12.120 --> 00:19:49.680
Three route families in this chapter. Percutaneous groups application to skin or mucous membranes; enteral delivers into the gastrointestinal tract, including oral, appropriate feeding-tube and rectal preparations; parenteral literally means outside the gut and commonly refers to injections. These broad groupings are not interchangeable product instructions. An oral suspension contains dispersed particles and may need the labeled mixing method; an emulsion disperses one liquid in another. The same millilitres of two formulations need not contain the same dose.
本章三类途径。经皮类归皮肤或黏膜应用，肠内进入胃肠道，含口服、适用喂养管和直肠制剂；肠外字面指胃肠外，通常指注射。这些大类不能替代具体产品说明。口服混悬液有分散粒子，可能需标签要求的混匀；乳剂是一种液分散在另一液。两剂型同毫升不必同药量。

00:19:49.680 --> 00:20:24.264
Read the prototype table as eight linked questions: class, mechanism, dose/route/timing, indication, desired effect, drug interactions, food interactions, and adverse effects/contraindications. A contraindication concerns a reason not to use a product in the situation; an interaction concerns another exposure changing its effect or risk. State what you expect to improve and what you must monitor, not only the treatment name. The table is a learning organizer, not a complete current monograph.
原型表可读成八组相联问题：分类、机制、量与途径时点、适应、预期作用、药物相互作用、食物相互作用、不良作用与禁忌。禁忌是此情境不宜使用的原因，相互作用是另一接触改作用或风险。应说明预期改善什么、须监什么，不只说治疗名。表是学习组织工具，非完整当前专论。

00:20:24.264 --> 00:21:01.248
A denominator check makes the model usable. For an invented60kg teaching adult at60% total-body-water, total water is36L: approximately24L intracellular and12L extracellular. The simplified extracellular split is about9L interstitial and3L plasma. These are model estimates, not a patient measurement or an infusion volume. Do not add the source's extra1% transcellular entry as though every rough percentage shared an exact denominator or formed a precise bedside prescription.
分母核查让模型可用。虚构60千克教学成人若总体水60%，水共36升：约24升细胞内、12升细胞外；简化外液约9升组织间、3升血浆。这是模型估计，不是患者实测或输液量。不能把来源另列1%跨细胞液直接相加，好像所有约数都同分母且能组成精密床边处方。

00:21:01.248 --> 00:21:38.304
Specialized spaces are still outside cells. Transcellular examples include cerebrospinal, pleural, peritoneal and joint fluids; they are specialized extracellular compartments, not fluid inside a cell. The source's separate-from-extracellular wording is misleading. Third spacing in clinical discussion usually concerns fluid sequestered away from useful circulation; it is not simply another name proving every normal transcellular space is pathological. Membrane structure, barriers and transport determine how each compartment communicates.
特殊空间仍在细胞外。跨细胞液例含脑脊液、胸膜、腹膜及关节液，属于特殊细胞外区隔，不是细胞内。来源称其独立于细胞外的措辞会误导。临床第三间隙丢失通常指液被隔在有效循环以外，不是说每个正常跨细胞空间都病理。膜、屏障及运输决定各区怎样交流。

00:21:38.304 --> 00:22:13.944
Equilibrium does not mean a dead membrane or identical solutes. Water can move in both directions while its net movement is zero. In a simple membrane system an opposing pressure difference can balance an osmotic tendency without identical solute concentrations. This is different from asserting that every living capillary has zero filtration. The glycocalyx, tissue-specific permeability and lymphatic drainage matter in real microvascular exchange; the source's universal filter-out/reabsorb-back picture is too simple.
平衡不等于膜停止活动或溶质全相同。水可双向移动而净移动为零。简单膜系统中，反向压力差能平衡渗透趋势，不必溶质同浓度。这不等于说每条活体毛细血管均零滤出。真实微血管交换还看糖萼、组织特异通透及淋巴回流，来源普遍一端滤出再全回吸图景过简。

00:22:13.944 --> 00:22:49.920
Apply feedback to the assigned examples. Rising temperature can activate sensing and heat-loss effectors that oppose the rise;37degrees in a schematic is not a universal diagnostic cutoff. Platelet recruitment can amplify a local clotting response. Suckling can drive oxytocin-mediated milk ejection, and cervical stretch can reinforce the childbirth contraction loop until delivery changes the stimulus. Positive means amplifying, not always beneficial; negative means opposing a deviation, not harmful.
把反馈用于指定例。体温上升可启动感受与散热效应来抵抗升高，图中37度非通用诊断界值。血小板募集可放大局部凝血，吸吮可驱动催产素介导排乳，宫颈牵张可强化分娩收缩环，直到娩出改变刺激。正指放大，不是总有益；负指抵抗偏离，不是有害。

00:22:49.920 --> 00:23:28.872
Question meaning matters more than a table label. The source questioning table mixes quality with provoking/relieving factors and duration with a previous similar episode. Ask both the present episode's length and recurrence separately. Family history can identify patterns and prompt further questions, but it does not prove a genetic cause from a few relatives. Genetic and inherited are not synonyms: most Down syndrome is not inherited, contrary to its unqualified placement among hereditary examples. Do not tell a family you have established inheritance during a paramedic history.
问题含义比表头重要。来源提问表把性质与诱发缓解、持续与既往类似发作混用，应分问当前持续多久及是否曾发。家族史可显模式、提示追问，却不能凭几个亲属就证遗传病因。遗传物质相关与由亲代传递并非同义；多数唐氏综合征不是家族遗传，来源不加限定地列作遗传实例会误导。不能在急救采史时告诉家属已确立遗传方式。

00:23:28.872 --> 00:24:19.464
Read the illustrated history/ROS forms as prompts, not completed findings. They group identity, reason for care, allergy reactions, actual medicines, past admissions/surgery, family/social exposures, nutrition and relevant skin, senses, mouth/neck, breathing, cardiac/vascular, gastrointestinal/urinary, reproductive, endocrine, musculoskeletal and neurological/mental symptoms. Ask sensitive questions only when relevant and with privacy. The ROS image mislabels vomiting blood as hemoptysis: hemoptysis is coughed blood, hematemesis vomited blood. Establish what the patient actually experienced and where blood appeared; do not infer the origin from a checkbox.
把图示病史及系统表当提示，不是已完成发现。其分身份、求助原因、过敏反应、实际药物、既往住院手术、家族社会接触、营养，以及相关皮肤、感官、口颈、呼吸、心血管、胃肠泌尿、生殖、内分泌、肌骨、神经精神症状。敏感问题须相关且保护隐私。ROS图把呕血错标hemoptysis：该词是咯血，呕血为hematemesis。应问真实经历及血从何出现，不能凭勾选推来源。

00:24:19.464 --> 00:24:58.944
Correct the infection-immunity shortcut. The source dialogue says a person with C. difficile cannot be infected again; that is false. Relapse or a new exposure can cause recurrence, so hand hygiene and transmission precautions still matter. Antibiotic resistance is not the same as spore formation, and colonization is not automatically symptomatic infection. The assigned summary also names active immunity: the person's own immune response develops after an appropriate exposure or immunization, rather than receiving ready-made antibodies. It does not mean immunity to every later infection.
纠正感染免疫捷径。来源对话说已有C. difficile就不会再感染，这是错误的；复发或新接触可致再次发病，手卫生及传播防护仍重要。抗生素耐药不等芽孢形成，定植不自动是有症状感染。指定总结也提主动免疫，即适当接触或免疫接种后，自身发展免疫反应，而非直接接收现成抗体；不表示对后来一切感染免疫。

00:24:58.944 --> 00:25:39.432
Match reprocessing to intended contact. Critical items enter sterile tissue or the vascular system and require sterilization. Semicritical items contact mucous membranes or nonintact skin and generally need at least high-level disinfection; noncritical items contact intact skin and need the applicable lower-level processing. Clean first, then use a validated method compatible with the device and local instructions. A named chemical, a hot temperature or an unbroken probe cover alone does not prove the required process was completed, and a disposable device is not made reusable by this table.
按预定接触分再处理。关键物品进入无菌组织或血管，需灭菌；半关键接触黏膜或不完整皮肤，通常至少高级消毒；非关键接触完整皮肤，需适用较低级处理。先清洁，再用符合器械和当地指令的经验证方法。某化学名、高温或完整探头套，本身都不证明已完成所需流程，表格也不能让一次性器械变可重复。

00:25:39.432 --> 00:26:27.096
Sterile setup and open gloving: rehearse the contact boundaries. Explain the task, clean hands, check package integrity/expiry and prepare a clean dry visible workspace with supplies within reach. Open the wrapper without touching its sterile centre; the source treats its2.5cm edge as unsterile. A bare hand touches only the inside folded cuff of the first glove. Once that hand is gloved, its sterile fingers lift the second glove beneath the folded cuff without contacting bare skin. Keep gloved hands visible and away from unsterile sleeves. If contact or sterility is uncertain, stop and replace the affected item; do not hide the breach.
无菌准备及开放戴手套：练接触边界。解释任务、清手、查包装完整有效期，备干净干燥可见工作区，物品可取。开包不触无菌中心，来源将边缘2.5厘米视为非无菌。裸手只触第一只手套翻折袖口内面，戴好后以无菌手指从第二只翻折袖口下提起，不碰裸皮肤。戴好双手保持可见、远离非无菌袖。接触或无菌性不明，停下换受影响物，不能掩盖破坏。

00:26:27.096 --> 00:27:04.440
Maintain the field while adding a solution. Verify the sealed product and expiry, protect the sterile receiving container and pour from the side without reaching an unsterile bottle or sleeve over the field. The source illustrates about15cm separation; avoid touching the receiving rim or splashing through the wrapper and follow the actual product/skill procedure, not distance alone. Distinguish wet contamination of a barrier from sterile liquid deliberately held in a sterile vessel. These are supervised learning principles, not authorization to perform an invasive procedure.
加液时维持无菌区。核封闭产品及有效期，保护无菌接收容器，从侧面倾倒，不把非无菌瓶或袖越过区域。来源示约15厘米间距，应避免触接收口缘或飞溅穿透包装，遵实际产品技能流程，不能只靠距离。区分屏障湿污染与故意装在无菌容器的无菌液体。这些是督导学习原则，不授权侵入操作。

00:27:04.440 --> 00:27:30.864
Cardiac output equals stroke volume times heart rate. At a fixed rate of 70/min, increasing stroke volume from 60 to 80 mL increases output from 4.2 to 5.6 L/min. The source sentence saying stroke volume and cardiac output are inversely related is incorrect; a slower rate may offset a higher stroke volume only when considering a similar total output.
心输出量等于每搏量乘心率。固定每分钟70次，每搏量从60增80毫升，输出由4.2增5.6升每分钟。来源“每搏量与心输出量反比”不正确；只有讨论相近总输出时，较慢心率可抵消较大每搏量。

00:27:30.864 --> 00:27:52.704
No palpable pulse is not synonymous with asystole. Ventricular fibrillation and pulseless electrical activity can also produce pulselessness. Follow the actual resuscitation assessment and rhythm pathway; a pulse finding cannot identify every electrical rhythm or justify declaring one from a textbook sentence.
摸不到脉不等于心静止，室颤及无脉电活动也可无脉。须按实际复苏评估及心律路径，脉发现不能识别所有电节律，不能凭书上一句下结论。

00:27:52.704 --> 00:28:21.840
15.6 - ordinary inspiration contracts and lowers the diaphragm, enlarging the thorax; quiet expiration largely follows relaxation and recoil. The source paragraph reverses contraction and relaxation and must not be memorized. Rate, rhythm, depth, work, air entry, mentation, oxygenation and appropriate capnography together assess respiratory function.
15.6——普通吸气是膈肌收缩下降、胸腔扩大，安静呼气主要为放松回缩。来源段落把收缩放松颠倒，不能背。频率节律深度、呼吸功、进气、意识、氧合及适当二氧化碳监测共同评估功能。

00:28:21.840 --> 00:28:50.016
15.7 - pressure needs the correct device, cuff, site, position and technique. The source cuff sentence reverses dimensions; the usual manual guide is bladder width about 40% of arm circumference and length 80-100%, with manufacturer fit marks controlling actual choice. It is not width covering 80% of shoulder-to-elbow length and a bladder encircling only 40%.
15.7——血压需正确设备、袖带、部位、体位及技术。来源袖带句把尺寸反了，通常手测气囊宽约臂围40%、长80%至100%，实际依厂家适合标记，不是宽占肩肘长80%且气囊只围40%。

00:28:50.016 --> 00:29:38.304
Temperature routes and blood-cell risks are not interchangeable. Oral measurement needs an appropriate sublingual site and a patient able to cooperate; recent food/drink/smoking, mouth breathing or oral injury can distort it. Axillary, temporal and tympanic devices measure different sites with device/age limitations; do not add a fixed correction to turn one route into another. The source's low-red-cell bleeding contraindication for rectal temperature confuses different blood-cell functions: platelet/bleeding risks and severe neutropenia need specific precautions. Rectal measurement also requires consent, training, indication and the approved procedure, not merely a textbook claim that it is accurate.
测温途径与不同血细胞风险不能混用。口测需适当舌下位置及能配合者；近期饮食吸烟、张口呼吸或口伤可干扰。腋、颞及耳测是不同部位，各有器械年龄限制，不能加固定差值把一种变另一种。来源以红细胞低说明肛测出血禁忌，混淆不同血细胞功能；血小板或出血风险及严重中性粒低须特定防护。肛测还需同意、训练、适应及获准流程，不只凭书称准确。

00:29:38.304 --> 00:30:12.456
Eleven systems, with structures and functions, part one. Skin in the integumentary system provides a barrier and contributes to temperature regulation. Bones support and protect, store minerals and house blood-forming marrow. Skeletal muscles move the body and generate heat. Brain, spinal cord and peripheral nerves integrate information and produce rapid responses. Endocrine glands, such as thyroid and pancreatic islets, release hormones that coordinate longer-ranging regulation.
十一系统的结构与功能，第一组：皮肤系统以皮肤形成屏障并参与体温调节；骨骼系统支持保护、储存矿物质并容纳造血骨髓；骨骼肌产生运动和热量；脑、脊髓与周围神经整合信息并产生快速反应；甲状腺、胰岛等内分泌结构释放激素，协调作用范围较广的调节。

00:30:12.456 --> 00:30:55.392
Eleven systems, part two. Heart and blood vessels transport blood, gases, nutrients, wastes and heat. Lymphatic vessels return tissue fluid; lymph nodes and spleen contribute to immune defence. Lungs exchange gases. Digestive organs, including stomach and intestines with support from liver and pancreas, process food and absorb nutrients. Kidneys and urinary passages regulate water, electrolytes and waste removal. Gonads and reproductive tracts produce gametes and hormones and support reproduction; anatomy is not an assumption about a person's gender, fertility or goals.
十一系统，第二组：心脏和血管运输血液、气体、营养、代谢废物和热量；淋巴管回收组织液，淋巴结与脾参与免疫防御；肺交换气体；胃肠在肝、胰支持下处理食物并吸收营养；肾及泌尿通路参与水、电解质调节和废物排出；性腺及生殖道生成配子、激素并支持繁殖。解剖结构不能用于假定个人性别认同、生育能力或意愿。

00:30:55.392 --> 00:31:29.208
Define directions before describing an injury. Anterior is toward the front and posterior toward the back; superior is toward the head and inferior toward the feet. Medial approaches the midline and lateral moves away from it. Proximal is nearer a limb's attachment and distal farther away; superficial is nearer the surface and deep farther inside. Patient right and left stay the patient's, even when you face them. Supine means face up and prone face down; neither changes the anatomical reference.
描述损伤前先定义方向：前侧朝身体前方，后侧朝后；上方朝头，下方朝足；内侧靠近中线，外侧远离中线；近端靠近肢体附着处，远端更远；浅靠近表面，深远离表面。即使面对患者，左右仍按患者自身。仰卧为面朝上，俯卧为面朝下，均不改变解剖参照。

00:31:29.208 --> 00:32:06.768
Map abdominal location from the patient's side. RUQ, LUQ, RLQ and LLQ mean right/left upper/lower quadrants; the dividing lines intersect at the umbilicus. The nine-region map has right hypochondriac, epigastric and left hypochondriac across the top; right lumbar, umbilical and left lumbar in the middle; right iliac or inguinal, hypogastric or pubic and left iliac or inguinal below. Location guides description, not a one-organ diagnosis: organs span regions and pain can be referred.
腹部定位按患者侧别。RUQ、LUQ、RLQ、LLQ分别为右上、左上、右下、左下象限，分界在脐部相交。九区上排为右季肋、腹上、左季肋；中排右腰、脐、左腰；下排右髂/腹股沟、腹下/耻骨、左髂/腹股沟。区域用于描述，不是一处对应一个诊断：器官可跨区，疼痛也可牵涉到别处。

00:32:06.768 --> 00:32:45.648
Laryngeal landmarks matter together. Thyroid and cricoid cartilages support the larynx; arytenoids move the true vocal folds, with vestibular or false folds above them and the epiglottis superiorly. Use glottis for the true-vocal-fold region and its opening, not as another name for the false folds: the assigned definition groups them too broadly. Airway protection depends on coordinated closure and elevation, not an epiglottis acting alone as an infallible lid. The trachea lies anterior to the esophagus, with C-shaped supports and a posterior muscular wall.
喉部标志要联系起来。甲状及环状软骨支撑喉；杓状软骨参与真声带运动，前庭襞/假声带在其上，会厌位于上方。声门应指真声带所在区域及开口，而不是假声带的别名；指定定义把它们归得过宽。气道保护依赖协调关闭和上提，不是会厌单独作为永不失灵的盖子。气管在食管前方，以C形软骨及后方肌性壁支撑。

00:32:45.648 --> 00:33:21.312
Trace one breath to the exchange surface: trachea, carina, right or left main bronchus, lobar bronchus, segmental bronchus, smaller bronchi, bronchioles and terminal bronchioles form the conducting route. Respiratory bronchioles, alveolar ducts, sacs and alveoli begin the exchange route. Bronchioles lack the large airway's cartilage supports and their smooth muscle changes caliber; parasympathetic activity tends toward constriction and sympathetic effects toward dilation. These are mechanisms, not permission for a drug or a dose.
追踪一口气至交换面：气管、隆嵴、左右主支气管、叶支气管、段支气管、更小支气管、细支气管和终末细支气管构成传导路线；呼吸性细支气管、肺泡管、囊及肺泡进入交换路线。细支气管没有大气道的软骨支撑，平滑肌能改变口径；副交感作用倾向收缩，交感效应倾向舒张。这些是机制，不是药物或剂量授权。

00:33:21.312 --> 00:34:02.376
Separate airflow pressure from lung-distending pressure. Let atmospheric pressure be the zero reference: alveolar pressure briefly below zero draws air inward, above zero drives it outward, and equality means no bulk flow. Transpulmonary pressure is alveolar minus pleural pressure; it is a different gradient that helps explain lung expansion. Boyle's inverse pressure-volume relation assumes a fixed gas quantity and temperature. The chapter's negative pleural values describe quiet spontaneous breathing approximately, not every forced expiration or positive-pressure breath; "pleural pressure" does not mean normal pleural air.
区分气流压差与肺扩张压差。把大气压作零参照：肺泡压短暂低于零使气流入，高于零使气流出，相等时无整体气流。跨肺压为肺泡压减胸膜压，是解释肺扩张的另一压差。波义耳压容反比关系假定气体量和温度固定。本章胸膜负压数值仅近似描述安静自主呼吸，不适用于每次用力呼气或正压呼吸；“胸膜压”不代表正常胸膜内有空气。

00:34:02.376 --> 00:34:41.016
Compare a stiff lung with a narrow airway. Low compliance means a smaller volume change for a given distending-pressure change; high resistance means more pressure difference is needed for a given flow. Surfactant reduces surface tension, while elastic recoil helps expiration. Quiet inspiration uses diaphragm and external intercostals; forced inspiration can recruit neck accessory muscles, and active forced expiration recruits abdominal and internal intercostal muscles. Similar visible effort can arise from different mechanisms, so the mechanism cannot be diagnosed from effort alone.
比较僵硬肺与狭窄气道。低顺应性表示相同扩张压变化只产生较小容积变化；高阻力表示相同气流需较大压差。表面活性物质降低表面张力，弹性回缩帮助呼气。安静吸气用膈肌及外肋间肌；用力吸气可动员颈部辅助肌，用力主动呼气可动员腹肌及内肋间肌。相似的费力外观可来自不同机制，不能只凭费力诊断。

00:34:41.016 --> 00:35:26.232
Volumes build capacities. Tidal volume is one ordinary breath; inspiratory reserve is extra air inhaled after an ordinary inspiration; expiratory reserve is extra air exhaled after ordinary expiration; residual volume remains after maximal expiration. IC equals tidal plus inspiratory reserve. VC equals inspiratory reserve plus tidal plus expiratory reserve. FRC equals expiratory reserve plus residual, and TLC equals VC plus residual. Simple expired-volume spirometry does not directly measure residual volume. Textbook average volumes are examples, not an individual ventilation target.
由肺容积组成肺容量。潮气量是一次普通呼吸量；吸气储备量是普通吸气后还能额外吸入的量；呼气储备量是普通呼气后还能额外呼出的量；残气量是最大呼气后仍留在肺内的量。深吸气量IC=潮气量+吸气储备量；肺活量VC=吸气储备量+潮气量+呼气储备量；功能残气量FRC=呼气储备量+残气量；肺总量TLC=VC+残气量。简单呼出量肺量计不能直接测残气量。教材平均值是示例，不是个体通气目标。

00:35:26.232 --> 00:36:13.272
Calculate effective ventilation, not rate alone. Minute ventilation equals tidal volume times respiratory rate. A simplified alveolar estimate is tidal volume minus dead-space volume, then multiplied by rate. For an original model with150mL dead space,480mL at15breaths per minute gives7.2L per minute total but4.95L alveolar. At240mL and30breaths, the same7.2L total gives only2.7L alveolar. Anatomical plus alveolar dead space make physiological dead space; poor perfusion can enlarge the latter. This arithmetic model is not a prescription for ventilation settings.
计算有效通气，而非只看频率。分钟通气量=潮气量×呼吸频率；简化肺泡通气估计为（潮气量－死腔量）×频率。原创模型设死腔150毫升：潮气量480毫升、每分钟15次，总通气7.2升/分，肺泡4.95升/分；240毫升、30次时总量同为7.2升，肺泡却只有2.7升。解剖死腔加肺泡死腔构成生理死腔；灌注不足可增加后者。这是算术模型，不是通气参数处方。

00:36:13.272 --> 00:36:57.384
Name the control inputs without inventing one master switch. The traditional table names medullary dorsal and ventral respiratory groups and a pontine respiratory group; their interacting network shapes rhythm and adjusts effort. Central chemoreceptors respond to CO2-related changes in central fluid acidity; carotid and aortic bodies sample arterial chemistry, including oxygen. Cortex contributes voluntary control, hypothalamus temperature and emotion, proprioceptors movement input, and airway irritant and inflation reflexes protective responses. The source's simplified group descriptions are not a literal on-off wiring diagram.
说出调节输入，不虚构一个总开关。传统表格列出延髓背侧、腹侧呼吸群及脑桥呼吸群；相互作用网络形成节律并调整呼吸功。中枢化学感受器感受与CO2有关的中枢液体酸度改变；颈动脉体和主动脉体感受动脉血化学情况，包括氧。皮层参与自主控制，下丘脑参与温度及情绪，本体感受器提供运动输入，气道刺激及肺膨胀反射提供保护。来源对各群的简化描述不是字面上的开关接线图。

00:36:57.384 --> 00:37:43.368
Finish the assigned sleep-apnea sidebar. Obstructive sleep apnea involves loss of upper-airway patency despite breathing effort; central apnea involves reduced respiratory drive and effort, and mixed patterns can occur. Snoring, witnessed pauses and daytime sleepiness prompt assessment, but are not a field diagnosis; sleep testing helps characterize the condition. CPAP applies continuous pressure to support airway patency. Contrary to the source's "regular intervals" wording, CPAP alone does not provide timed mandatory breaths or replace ventilation for a person who cannot breathe adequately. Other pressure-support devices and acute EMS indications require their own protocols.
补完指定睡眠呼吸暂停侧栏。阻塞型是在仍有呼吸努力时上气道不通畅；中枢型涉及呼吸驱动及努力减少，也可混合。打鼾、目击停呼吸及白天嗜睡提示需要评估，但不是院前确诊；睡眠检查有助分类。CPAP以持续压力支持气道通畅。来源所写“定时间隔”并不准确：单纯CPAP不提供定时强制呼吸，也不能替代无足够自主呼吸者所需通气。其他压力支持装置及急救适应证须按各自流程。

00:37:43.368 --> 00:38:28.728
The final gas-exchange opening introduces partial pressure: each gas contributes part of a mixture's total pressure, and those contributions add to the total. In an original dry-air model,21% oxygen at700mmHg contributes147mmHg, compared with about160mmHg at760mmHg. These are dry inspired-gas calculations, not alveolar oxygen, PaO2 or an oximeter percentage. Humidification, alveolar CO2, exchange and blood flow change the subsequent stages. The assignment ends during this introduction; the rest of22.4 is not silently added as a required reading.
最后的气体交换开头引入分压：每种气体贡献混合气体总压的一部分，各分压相加等于总压。原创干燥空气模型中，氧21%、总压700毫米汞柱时氧分压为147；总压760时约160。这是干燥吸入气计算，不是肺泡氧、PaO2或血氧仪百分比。湿化、肺泡CO2、交换和血流还会改变后续环节。指定范围在导言中途结束，不把22.4其余内容偷偷加成指定阅读。

00:38:28.728 --> 00:38:58.968
1.2 Risk factors are not destiny. Biological susceptibility, illness, brain injury, disrupted sleep, medicines, substance use, trauma, loss, conflict, discrimination and material insecurity can interact. A factor may be modifiable by services or policy, not personal willpower alone. Do not turn a population association into an individual diagnosis or claim a simple neurotransmitter imbalance has been measured from behaviour.
1.2 风险因素不是命运。生物易感性、疾病、脑损伤、睡眠紊乱、药物、物质使用、创伤、丧失、冲突、歧视及物质生活不安全可相互作用。有些因素需要通过服务或政策改变，不是只靠个人意志。不能把群体关联当成个体诊断，也不能声称已从行为测出某种简单的神经递质失衡。

00:38:58.968 --> 00:39:37.512
Repair the modifiable-barrier shortcut. Section3.2 calls cost, access and support nonmodifiable because they may be outside the individual's immediate control. They are not necessarily fixed: a service can sometimes arrange interpretation, a reachable appointment, transport or another resource. Conversely, an attitude is not always freely or instantly changeable. Ask what prevented the agreed plan and who can help change it. The book's help-seeking pathway means the route a person takes toward assistance, not a mandatory single referral sequence.
纠正“不可改变障碍”的简化。3.2把费用、可及及支持称不可改变，是说可能不在个体即时控制内，不表示永远固定：服务有时可安排口译、可到的预约、交通或其他资源。反过来，态度也不是总能自由即时改变。应问什么阻碍约定计划、谁能协助改变。书中求助路径指个人取得帮助的路线，不是强制唯一转介顺序。

00:39:37.512 --> 00:40:19.272
Use the proxemic model without turning distance into consent. The text's descriptive zones are intimate, contact to18inches; personal,1-4feet; social,4-12feet; public,more than12feet. They are a teaching model, not universal cultural boundaries or an ambulance positioning rule. Ask what proximity feels acceptable, explain clinically necessary touch, expose only what is needed and provide realistic choices. A quiet person or a nod has not automatically agreed to examination; distress does not have to disappear before respectful urgent care can proceed.
使用空间距离模型，但不把距离当同意。教材描述亲密距离为接触至18英寸，个人1-4英尺，社交4-12英尺，公众超过12英尺。它们是教学模型，不是通用文化界线或救护车摆位规则。应询问可接受靠近、解释必要触碰、仅暴露所需并给真实选择。安静或点头不自动等于同意查体；尊重的紧急照护也不须等痛苦完全消失。

00:40:19.272 --> 00:40:48.672
Replace barriers. Jargon, interruptions, irrelevant personal questions, blaming demands for justification, moral judgments, subject changes, minimization and false reassurance can close discussion. Replace blame with a neutral request to describe what happened. Replace everything will be fine with an honest next step. Relevant direct safety questions remain appropriate; respect does not mean avoiding a necessary assessment.
替换沟通障碍。术语、打断、无关的私人问题、责备式要求解释、道德评判、转移话题、轻视及虚假安慰，都可能让谈话关闭。把责备改为中性地请对方描述经过；把一切都会好改为诚实的下一步。相关的直接安全问题仍然适当：尊重不等于回避必要评估。

00:40:48.672 --> 00:41:16.464
Johari self-awareness. Open/arena is known to self and others; hidden/facade is known to self but not others; blind is known to others but not self; unknown is known to neither. Specific feedback can reveal a blind spot such as explaining too quickly. Behaviour already observed by colleagues is not automatically unknown. Learning does not require sharing private trauma or every hidden feeling.
Johari自我觉察模型。开放区是自己和他人都知道；隐藏区是自己知道、他人不知道；盲区是他人知道、自己不知道；未知区是双方都不知道。具体反馈可揭示解释太快等盲点。已被同事观察到的行为不能自动归入未知区。学习不要求披露私人创伤或每一种隐藏感受。

00:41:16.464 --> 00:41:43.128
Gibbs reflection connects experience and action. Describe the event; identify relevant feelings; evaluate what helped/hindered; analyze why; conclude what could change; develop an action plan. Use an observable interaction and specific improvement, not a verdict that you are good or bad. Check the patient perspective and evidence, then test the proposed change in later practice.
Gibbs反思把经历连接到行动：描述事件，识别相关感受，评价哪些有助或有碍，分析原因，总结可以改变什么，并制定行动计划。应聚焦可观察的互动及具体改进，而不是判自己好或坏。核对患者视角和证据，再在后续练习中检验改动。

00:41:43.128 --> 00:42:28.896
One worked reasoning cycle uses both kinds of safety. In an original rehearsal, a patient after a bicycle fall reports fear and worries that staff will dismiss a previous psychiatric diagnosis. Recognize the report plus actual breathing, movement and perfusion findings; analyze possible injury and physical causes without deciding it is only panic. Prioritize immediate threats while explaining your actions; agree on an achievable assessment step, use the authorized school approach, then reassess the observed response. A calmer voice alone does not prove that ventilation or injury risk is resolved. Transfer unresolved concerns as well as what improved.
一个完整推理环同时顾两类安全。原创演练中，骑车跌倒者说害怕，并担心工作人员因既往精神诊断忽视自己。识别其报告及真实呼吸、活动和灌注发现；分析可能伤情及躯体原因，不先定仅惊恐。解释行动同时先处理即时威胁；协商可行评估一步，按获准学校方法行动，再复评真实反应。声音平静本身不证明通气或损伤风险解决；交接既报改善，也报未解担忧。

00:42:28.896 --> 00:43:11.520
Time scale does not remove the evaluation loop. The assigned acute and extended tables illustrate the same sequence: cues, interpretation, priorities, a justified plan, actual actions and measured outcomes. Do not copy their hospital injection, room restriction, camera observation or medication-timing example into a PCP plan. Four-hour observations and hourly rounding are not continuous physiological monitoring or an EMS reassessment interval. Choose timely reassessment from the actual risk and current protocol, document the method and outcome, and revise or escalate rather than call a partly achieved goal complete.
时间尺度不取消评价环。指定急性与长期表展示同序：线索、解释、优先、合理计划、实际行动及可测结局。不能把医院注射、房间限制、摄像观察或改服药时间例抄进PCP计划。四小时测量、每小时巡视不等连续生理监测，也非救护复评间隔。应依实际风险和现行流程及时复评，记方法结果，修改或升级，不把部分达成说成全达成。

00:43:11.520 --> 00:43:40.608
Turn curiosity into a usable question. PICOT specifies the population/problem, intervention, comparison, outcome and time. An original learning question is whether a structured handover prompt, compared with usual unprompted practice, reduces omitted allergy information during simulated transfers over four practice sessions. Its outcome is not automatically better survival; measure what the design actually tests.
把好奇转成可回答的问题。PICOT明确群体或问题、干预、比较、结局和时间。原创学习问题是：四次模拟转交练习中，结构化交接提示相比无提示的通常做法，能否减少过敏信息遗漏？所测结果不自动等于生存改善；应测量设计真正能检验的指标。

00:43:40.608 --> 00:44:23.352
Make a SMART aim and test it. Specific names exactly what will change; measurable identifies a count or observation; achievable fits people and resources; relevant connects to the real need; time-bound sets when to review. An original simulation aim is to reduce omitted allergy information across four practice sessions without delaying the critical report. Ask what you want to achieve, how you will recognize improvement and what change to try. Plan predicts; Do tests; Study compares result with prediction; Act adapts, adopts or abandons and plans the next test. Do not label all changed numbers an improvement.
制定SMART目标并检验。Specific明确改变什么；Measurable确定计数或观察；Achievable符合人员资源；Relevant联系真实需要；Time-bound约定何时复查。原创模拟目标是在四次练习中减少过敏信息遗漏，同时不拖延关键报告。应问想达到什么、怎样认出改善、准备试什么改变。Plan作预测，Do测试，Study比较结果与预测，Act调整、采纳或放弃并安排下一轮。数值发生改变不自动等于改善。

00:44:23.352 --> 00:44:59.448
Treat the EBP example table as conditional. Head elevation, repositioning, PPE and oxygen each require the actual indication, patient tolerance, contraindications and current protocol. A generic thirty to forty-five degree bed angle, two-hour turning example or statement about oxygen and COPD is not a universal patient order. It also does not establish that every person with COPD needs continuous oxygen. Link an action to a justified goal and monitor benefit and harm rather than performing every table item.
循证示例表需要条件。抬高头部、翻身、PPE及氧疗都要看实际适应证、耐受、禁忌和现行流程。泛用30-45度床头、两小时翻身示例，或关于COPD与氧气的表述，都不是通用医嘱，也不证明每位COPD患者都需要持续氧疗。应把行动联系到合理目标并监测获益和伤害，而不是把表中项目全部做一遍。

00:44:59.448 --> 00:45:44.088
Do not transplant the U.S. DNR anecdote. A patient's resuscitation preference, a valid No CPR medical order, a MOST and an advance directive are related but distinct. The textbook story about filing a patient-signed form is not a complete BC validation procedure. Current HealthLinkBC distinguishes No CPR from other care, and BCEHS R04 directs consultation when the appropriate intervention or whether to start CPR is uncertain. No CPR does not mean no comfort, symptom relief or all other indicated care. Check the actual document and current authorized process; do not create, override or infer an order from the story.
不能移植美国DNR轶事。患者复苏意愿、有效No CPR医疗医嘱、MOST及预先指示彼此有关，但并不相同。教材把患者签署表格归档的故事，不是完整卑诗有效性核查程序。现行HealthLinkBC区分不做CPR与其他照护，BCEHS R04要求在适当干预或是否开始CPR不确定时咨询。不做CPR不等于不提供舒适、症状缓解或其他有适应照护。应核实际文件和获准现行程序，不能根据故事自行建立、推翻或推定医嘱。

00:45:44.088 --> 00:46:31.272
Validate a unit conflict before interpreting a chart. The assigned printed page 173 example pairs89.3 degrees Fahrenheit with38.5 degrees Celsius; they cannot be equivalent. Celsius equals Fahrenheit minus 32, multiplied by five ninths:89.3 F is about31.8 C, while38.5 C is101.3 F. Do not choose one as the patient's true temperature from arithmetic alone. Recheck the original measurement, route/device and record, preserve the discrepancy and repeat appropriately while assessing the patient. This is source error detection, not an answer to the textbook case questions.
解释病历前先核单位冲突。指定印刷173页示例把华氏89.3度与摄氏38.5度并列，两者不等。摄氏=（华氏－32）×5/9：89.3华氏约为31.8摄氏，而38.5摄氏为101.3华氏。仅靠算术不能选定哪一个是患者真体温。应核原测量、途径设备及记录，保留矛盾，边评估患者边适当复测。这是来源纠错，不是教材病例题答案。

00:46:31.272 --> 00:47:13.680
The vascular cold-limb sign is not a core-temperature diagnosis. The classic six-P description includes pain, pallor, pulselessness, paresthesia, paralysis and poikilothermia: here the affected limb is unusually cold or takes on ambient temperature with poor blood supply. The assigned parenthesis about inability to regulate core temperature misstates this local context. New pain, coolness or sensory/motor loss can be urgent even without all six signs. Compare sides and baseline, assess promptly and escalate through the current school/service approach; do not wait for the complete mnemonic.
血管评估中的肢体冷，不是核心体温诊断。经典六P包括疼痛、苍白、无脉、感觉异常、瘫痪及poikilothermia；此处指供血不良时患肢异常冷或温度趋近环境。指定段括号所写无法调节核心温度，误述了这个局部语境。即使六项未齐，新出现疼痛、冷或感觉运动丧失也可紧迫。应比较双侧和基线，及时评估，按学校及现行服务方法升级，不等口诀凑齐。

00:47:13.680 --> 00:47:54.768
Read the NCJMM layers as a measurement framework, not a rigid bedside script. Broad clinical decisions and judgment are unpacked into forming, refining and evaluating hypotheses; the directly measurable six functions sit in layer 3, and contextual influences in layer 4. Show the work: identify a real cue, explain its meaning, compare competing risks, choose a justified authorized action and evaluate the observed response. A normal finding can be relevant evidence. The source's claims of universal superiority or a replacement for ADPIE go beyond NCSBN's stated purpose.
把NCJMM层次读作测量框架，不是床边硬性脚本。广义临床决定和判断可拆成形成、修正及评价假设；可直接测量的六项功能在第3层，背景影响在第4层。要展示实际工作：找真实线索、解释含义、比较竞争风险、选择合理获准行动、评价观察反应。正常发现也可能是相关证据。来源声称普遍更优或取代ADPIE，超出了NCSBN所述目的。

00:47:54.768 --> 00:48:35.424
Use active retrieval to reveal a reasoning gap. Close the reading, reconstruct the six-function chain in your own words, then apply it to one unfamiliar original case. Explain one cue, a competing explanation, the missing information that matters, a permitted next step and the response you will reassess. Reopen the guide, correct the specific omission, then try again without looking on another occasion. Fluency while rereading is not evidence of unaided recall. This is an original study routine for the school's Active Retrieval focus, not an official scoring rubric or exam prediction.
用主动提取暴露推理缺口。合上阅读，用自己的话重建六功能环，再用于一个不熟悉的原创案例。解释一条线索、一个竞争解释、关键缺失资料、权限内下一步及将复评的反应。重开指南，修正具体遗漏，之后换个时机再不看材料重试。重读时感觉流畅，不证明能独立回忆。这是针对学校Active Retrieval重点的原创学习方法，不是官方评分表或押题。

00:48:35.424 --> 00:49:37.632
Do not silently reconcile Table7.5 with Table7.1. Table7.5 gives pulse rates per minute of120-180 for preterm infants,100-160 for newborns0-1month,80-140 for infants1-12months,80-130 for toddlers1-3years,80-110 for preschoolers3-5years,70-100 for school age6-12years, and60-100 for adolescents13-18years and adults. Compare the actual infant values with Table7.1's100-180: the difference is real, not a transcription you should hide. Identify the specified table or school reference in an exam question; in patient care, assess state, method, symptoms and trend instead of choosing whichever table makes a finding look normal.
不要悄悄合并表7.5与表7.1。表7.5的脉率单位为次/分：早产儿120至180；0至1个月新生儿100至160；1至12个月婴儿80至140；1至3岁幼儿80至130；3至5岁学龄前儿童80至110；6至12岁学龄儿童70至100；13至18岁青少年与成人60至100。对比表7.1的婴儿100至180，两表确实不同，不能隐去这个差异。考试应识别题目指定的表格或学校参考；照护时结合状态、方法、症状及趋势，不要挑一张能把异常说成正常的表。

00:49:37.632 --> 00:50:27.096
Table7.3 separates temperature routes. This source lists oral35.8-37.3 C, axillary34.8-36.3, tympanic36.1-37.9 and rectal36.8-38.0. Keep these values tied to FON Table7.3: another assigned book may use different intervals, and even this book's age table uses a different oral interval. A labelled reference range is not a validated fever decision rule for every age. In particular, it must not reassure you about a young infant at a recognized fever threshold. Record the actual route and device; do not convert a route using a fixed offset.
表7.3区分测温部位：本来源列口温35.8至37.3°C、腋温34.8至36.3、鼓膜温度36.1至37.9、直肠温度36.8至38.0。这些数值必须带上FON表7.3的来源标签；其他指定书籍可能采用不同范围，本书年龄表的口温范围也不同。参考范围不等于适用于所有年龄的已验证发热判断规则，尤其不能用它否定小婴儿已经达到公认发热阈值的风险。记录真实测量部位与设备，不要用固定偏移量转换部位。

00:50:27.096 --> 00:51:18.264
Correct a temperature-difference error on printed279. The book pairs a0.3-0.6 C difference with32.5-33.1 F higher, incorrectly applying the absolute-temperature offset. For an absolute reading, F equals1.8 times C plus32. For a difference, delta F equals1.8 times delta C, with no plus32: a0.3-0.6 C difference is0.54-1.08 F. This repairs the arithmetic, not the clinical claim that every ear reading is predictably higher than every oral reading. Device, positioning and patient factors still prevent a universal route-conversion rule.
纠正印刷279页的温差换算错误。教材把高0.3至0.6°C对应成高32.5至33.1°F，错误地把绝对温度的偏移量用于温差。绝对读数换算为°F＝1.8×°C＋32；温差则为Δ°F＝1.8×Δ°C，不加32。因此0.3至0.6°C的温差对应0.54至1.08°F。这个计算修复只纠正算术，并不能证明每次耳温都固定高于每次口温。设备、定位及患者因素意味着不存在通用的部位转换公式。

00:51:18.264 --> 00:51:58.560
Relate cuff dimensions to the arm, not the cloth label alone. The source describes bladder width near40percent of arm circumference and bladder length80-100percent; these refer to the inflatable bladder, not the whole outer fabric. Follow the actual manufacturer's fit markings. A cuff that does not fit can bias the result. The reading defines an orthostatic fall as at least20 mmHg systolic or10 diastolic within three minutes of standing. A high-risk or unstable patient should not be stood up merely to produce this measurement; assessment safety and the actual protocol come first.
把袖带尺寸与臂围联系起来，而不是只看布套名称。教材描述充气囊宽约为臂围的40%，长度为80%至100%；这里指充气囊，不是整个外层布套。实际应遵循厂家适配标识，尺寸不合可能造成测量偏差。阅读将体位性下降描述为站立3分钟内收缩压至少下降20mmHg或舒张压至少下降10mmHg。不能只为取得这个结果而让不稳定或高风险患者站起来；评估安全及实际操作规范优先。

00:51:58.560 --> 00:52:37.200
The actual assigned section 2.6 begins with observation, not a coma score alone. Notice general appearance, interaction, level of alertness, eye/nose drainage, facial symmetry and access to glasses, contacts or hearing aids. Ask what is new and compare the person's baseline. An unkempt appearance is a reason to ask about function and support, not proof of neglect; limited eye contact can have cultural or personal explanations. A new change in consciousness or facial movement requires timely assessment rather than a psychiatric label from appearance.
实际指定的2.6从观察开始，不只是计算昏迷评分。注意一般外观、互动、清醒程度、眼鼻分泌物、面部对称，以及眼镜、隐形眼镜或助听器是否可用。询问哪些变化是新出现的，并比较个人基线。衣着不整提示应询问功能与支持，不证明被忽视；眼神接触少也可能有文化或个人原因。新出现的意识或面部运动改变需要及时评估，不能仅凭外观贴上精神疾病标签。

00:52:37.200 --> 00:53:06.432
Use non-testable rather than inventing a response. The source's older C/E/T suffixes differ from the official structured GCS aid's NT. Swelling, an airway device, paralysis or another barrier may prevent testing; record the reason, not an automatic 1 or a fabricated complete total. Protect the airway and investigate deterioration regardless of a convenient score; reassess both sides and the trend.
无法测试时应记录无法测试，不要编造反应。来源较早的C、E、T后缀与官方结构化GCS辅助表的NT不同。肿胀、气道装置、瘫痪或其他障碍可能妨碍测试，应记录原因，而不是自动记1分或虚构完整总分。不论分数是否看起来方便，都应保护气道并调查恶化，复评两侧表现与趋势。

00:53:06.432 --> 00:53:44.328
Make sample quality explicit. Check the actual meter, compatible unexpired strips, storage conditions and required quality control before use. Clean the sampling site and let it dry completely; contamination or wet preparation can distort the sample. Use an appropriate finger-side site and a safe single-use lancet. Forceful milking can introduce tissue fluid or damage the sample. Apply the required volume as the device instructs; do not smear it, invent a number from an error display or treat every first-versus-second-drop rule as universal.
把样本质量说清楚。使用前核对实际血糖仪、兼容且未过期的试纸、储存条件及所需质控。清洁采样部位并完全待干，污染或尚湿的准备液会影响样本。采用适当指侧部位及安全的一次性采血针。用力挤揉可能混入组织液或损伤样本。按设备说明给予所需血量，不涂抹，不把报错屏幕编成数字，也不要把首滴或第二滴规则当成通用要求。

00:53:44.328 --> 00:54:21.648
Prevent bloodborne transfer during assisted monitoring. A fingerstick device must never be shared between people, even if someone proposes changing its lancet. For assisted testing, use the appropriate single-use auto-disabling device. If a professional meter is shared, clean and disinfect it after each use exactly as its manufacturer permits; an ordinary home meter is not automatically suitable. Separate unused supplies from used equipment, dispose of the lancet at the point of use, change contaminated gloves and clean hands before touching clean supplies.
协助测血糖时防止血源传播。采血装置不能多人共用，即使有人提议更换针头也不行；协助检测应采用适当的一次性自动失效装置。共用专业血糖仪时，每次使用后按厂家允许的方法清洁和消毒，普通家用仪器不自动适合共用。把未用物资与已用设备分开，在使用处立即弃针，换掉污染手套，并在触碰清洁物资前清洁双手。

00:54:21.648 --> 00:55:14.880
Build the actual ATMIST AMBO report. A is age and identity; T is onset or injury time; M is mechanism or medical complaint; I is injuries and examination findings; S is signs, including vital-sign trends and GCS; T is treatment and response. AMBO adds allergies with reactions, medication, relevant medical/social/family background and other important information. SBAR instead organizes a consultation as situation, background, assessment and recommendation or requested decision. Confirm the patient identity and receiving responsibility; promptly raise any identifier mismatch. A quiet 20-30-second critical handover is conditional on immediate safety, not a reason to stop necessary care.
组织真正的ATMIST AMBO交接：A为年龄与身份，T为起病或受伤时间，M为机制或内科主诉，I为损伤和检查发现，S为体征、趋势及GCS，T为治疗和反应。AMBO再补充过敏及反应、用药、相关医学社会家族背景，以及其他重要信息。SBAR则把咨询组织为当前情况、背景、评估及建议或所请求的决定。核对患者身份和接收责任，发现身份不一致时立即提出。危重交接尽量安静20至30秒的前提是即时安全，不应因此停止必要照护。

00:55:14.880 --> 00:55:57.984
Original handover practice: An older adult became unwell two hours ago and is now confused and breathing rapidly. Pressure has fallen from 112/70 to 92/58; pulse has risen from 104 to 122. Give the measured oxygen setting and saturation, relevant examination, actual support and response, then allergy reactions, medicines and background. State that deterioration is continuing and identify the immediate help required. Do not hide a falling trend because the latest systolic remains above 90. Pause for the receiving team to clarify and explicitly accept responsibility.
原创交接练习：一名老年人两小时前开始不适，现在意识混乱且呼吸加快。血压从112/70降到92/58，脉率从104升到122。报告实测供氧条件和饱和度、相关检查、实际支持及反应，再补充过敏反应、用药和背景。明确说明病情仍在恶化，并指出立即需要的帮助。不能因最新收缩压仍高于90就隐瞒下降趋势。给接收团队澄清的机会，并明确确认其接收照护责任。

00:55:57.984 --> 00:57:01.200
Use the adult prehospital Table 2 rather than guessing what abnormal means. Its 15-minute column includes pulse below 50 or above 110/min, systolic pressure below 90 mmHg, respirations below 10 or above 24/min, saturation below 94 percent despite oxygen/CPAP, increased breathing effort, GCS below 15 and glucose below 4 during treatment, as well as treatment/medication or listed concerning symptoms. Active resuscitation, impending cardiovascular/respiratory failure and the first 10 minutes after arrest are in its 2-5-minute column; the prose also discusses 2-3 minutes during shock resuscitation. Table 2 separately notes hourly glucose after symptom-free recovery above 4, unless symptoms return; that is not non-conveyance clearance. These are setting-labelled monitoring instructions, never a reason to wait when the patient changes.
使用成人院前表2，不要猜测异常的含义。其15分钟栏包括脉率低于50或高于110次/分、收缩压低于90mmHg、呼吸低于10或高于24次/分、给氧或CPAP下饱和度仍低于94%、呼吸功增加、GCS低于15、治疗过程中血糖低于4，以及接受治疗用药或列出的高风险症状。积极复苏、即将发生循环或呼吸衰竭及骤停后最初10分钟列入2至5分钟栏，正文还讨论休克复苏时2至3分钟。表2另注明：低血糖纠正后无症状、血糖高于4时可每小时复测，症状复现则例外；这不等于符合不转运条件。这些是有情境标签的监测要求，不能成为患者改变时继续等待的理由。

00:57:01.200 --> 00:57:52.248
Do not blend consolidated-care Table 1 into Table 2. Table 1 uses saturation below 90 percent despite oxygen and GCS below 13, with temperature below 35 or above 38 C, alongside pulse below 50/above 110, pressure below 90 and respirations below 10/above 24. Its 15-minute symptom list includes chest pain, ischemic/unstable ECG changes, dyspnea, altered mentation, concerning behavior, abdominal pain despite analgesia, spinal restriction and major trauma; others are in the 30-minute column. Its hourly glucose note for below 4 or above 12 is not permission to postpone correction of a low. State the setting and escalate from the actual findings.
不要把整合照护表1与表2拼在一起。表1采用给氧下饱和度低于90%、GCS低于13及体温低于35或高于38°C，另有脉率低于50或高于110、血压低于90、呼吸低于10或高于24。其15分钟症状栏列胸痛、缺血或不稳定心电变化、气促、意识改变、需关注行为、镇痛后仍腹痛、脊柱活动限制及重大创伤；其他患者在30分钟栏。对血糖低于4或高于12的每小时复测备注，不允许延迟纠正低血糖。说明实际环境，并依据真实发现升级。

00:57:52.248 --> 00:58:06.744
Prepare to explain the seven assigned module domains, perform the school assessment sequence and interpret actual observations. Use the full lectures and paired reading explanations rather than a fact-only checklist.
应准备解释七个指定模块领域，实施学校评估顺序并解释实际观察。使用完整讲授和对照阅读，而不是只有事实的勾选表。

00:58:06.744 --> 00:58:21.000
Practise the school case types with original simulation information, including an unresponsive prone patient and an older person after a fall. Do not memorize a fabricated answer as though it were the assessed case.
以原创模拟信息练习学校案例类型，包括俯卧无反应者及老年跌倒者。不能把虚构答案当考核案例答案来背。

00:58:21.000 --> 00:58:33.024
Your first PCR must be your own record of what was actually observed and done. We provide a blank aid and demonstration method, not a completed school submission or quiz response.
第一份 PCR 必须是你对实际观察和行动的自写记录。我们提供空白辅助及示范方法，不提供完成的学校提交件或测验答案。

00:58:33.024 --> 00:58:46.200
The school reading locators remain visible below, including unresolved revision or extent issues. Teaching the confirmed material continues while those source gaps are retained, not hidden.
下方保留学校阅读位置，包括尚未解决的版本及范围问题。确认材料继续教学，来源缺口则保留而非隐藏。
